<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Pius V</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1504–1572</span> · Also known as Antonio Ghislieri</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pope Pius V, a Dominican and former inquisitor, reigned from 1566 to 1572 and enforced the decrees of the Council of Trent. In 1569 he raised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cosimo-i-de-medici">Cosimo I de' Medici</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duke-of-tuscany">Grand Duke of Tuscany</a>, in 1570 he excommunicated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I of England</a>, and he organised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-league-1571">Holy League</a> whose fleet won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lepanto">Battle of Lepanto</a> in 1571.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-pius-v.jpg" alt="Pope Pius V" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bartolomeo Passarotti and workshop · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bartolomeo_Passarotti_-_Pius_V.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
